WEBVTT

00:01.087 --> 00:02.257
[SUMITA] Satisfy,

00:02.797 --> 00:06.597
the VR game phenomenon often
referred to as "another Earth."

00:07.677 --> 00:09.807
Today, we'll be talking
with two experts

00:09.887 --> 00:12.647
about what makes each
of the game's jobs so special

00:12.727 --> 00:15.647
and open a discussion
on the function of classes.

00:17.317 --> 00:19.197
Now, class is more
than just a title.

00:19.277 --> 00:22.657
It has a massive impact on how
powerful a player can become.

00:22.737 --> 00:25.947
Yura, what would you say makes
job selection so important?

00:26.037 --> 00:27.367
[YURA] Well, Sumita,

00:27.447 --> 00:29.747
it is true that some jobs
are naturally stronger

00:29.827 --> 00:31.747
and have more useful skills,

00:31.827 --> 00:32.957
but what matters most is

00:33.037 --> 00:34.957
how well you master
the one you choose.

00:35.037 --> 00:35.997
[Roy scoffs]

00:36.087 --> 00:37.457
Yeah, you say that,

00:37.547 --> 00:39.587
but it's pretty obvious
you're jealous of us players

00:39.667 --> 00:41.007
with special classes.

00:41.087 --> 00:42.087
You may be popular,

00:42.177 --> 00:43.927
but you're still
just a Black Mage.

00:44.677 --> 00:46.217
Too bad for you, sweetheart,

00:46.307 --> 00:49.097
but rare trumps normal
and epic trumps rare.

00:49.177 --> 00:51.347
The game's all about
how high your numbers are.

00:51.977 --> 00:53.847
And I'm living proof.

00:55.437 --> 00:58.397
Oh!
Roy has drawn his sword, folks!

00:58.987 --> 01:01.487
I was doing well before,
but once I went Epic,

01:01.567 --> 01:04.617
it was a luxury ride
straight to the top 100.

01:04.697 --> 01:05.907
[smirks]

01:05.987 --> 01:08.737
Oh, I'm quite familiar
with the Blood Warrior.

01:08.827 --> 01:11.867
Your class has a passive skill
that drains your opponent's HP.

01:11.957 --> 01:13.037
Huh.

01:13.117 --> 01:14.327
Didn't know you were such a fan.

01:14.417 --> 01:15.497
[YURA] So basically,

01:15.587 --> 01:17.747
you're carried
by your class and gear.

01:17.837 --> 01:19.417
That does sound
awfully luxurious.

01:19.507 --> 01:22.047
-What's that, bitch?
-[SUMITA] Okay, moving on!

01:22.127 --> 01:25.177
Our next topic
is Satisfy's epic classes.

01:25.257 --> 01:26.597
Currently, there are three.

01:26.677 --> 01:29.017
And Roy here
has obtained one of those three,

01:29.097 --> 01:30.347
-the Blood Warrior.
-[smirks]

01:30.427 --> 01:32.017
The second is held by Agnes,

01:32.097 --> 01:34.557
the number-seven player,
who has asked Satisfy News

01:34.647 --> 01:36.567
to keep those details
confidential.

01:37.187 --> 01:39.147
And as for the mysterious
third player,

01:39.227 --> 01:41.147
there is not one
shred of evidence

01:41.237 --> 01:42.647
as to who it could be!

01:42.737 --> 01:44.487
What kind of class
could they have?

01:44.567 --> 01:46.817
Rumor has it there are rare
and normal ones

01:46.907 --> 01:48.867
that don't rely
on combat at all!

01:49.487 --> 01:52.787
Combat or non-combat,
which users and which classes

01:52.867 --> 01:55.577
will change the history
of Satisfy forever?

01:55.667 --> 01:57.247
Stay tuned to find out.

01:57.337 --> 01:58.497
Back to studio.

01:59.087 --> 02:01.047
[♪ opening theme song playing]

03:32.007 --> 03:34.177
Glad you were able
to get patched up so quick.

03:34.267 --> 03:36.887
I must say,
meeting a young lad like you

03:36.977 --> 03:39.687
makes me think this world
might be all right after all.

03:39.767 --> 03:41.187
You know, without my help,

03:41.267 --> 03:43.437
you would've never
even made it to the doctor.

03:43.517 --> 03:44.727
Yes, that's true.

03:44.817 --> 03:46.357
No need to thank me.

03:46.447 --> 03:49.237
But you could reward me with
that sweet-ass hunk of metal.

03:49.317 --> 03:51.407
Yes, that's true. Mm?

03:51.487 --> 03:53.447
Huh? Wait, no, it isn't!

03:53.537 --> 03:54.697
I can't give you that!

03:54.787 --> 03:55.947
[TAKUMI] What the hell, man?!

03:56.037 --> 03:58.037
Don't be a dick,
I saved your life!

03:58.117 --> 03:59.117
Without me,
you woulda been murdered

03:59.207 --> 04:00.497
by those Mero mouth-breathers!

04:00.577 --> 04:02.747
I understand that,
but they are heirlooms.

04:02.837 --> 04:04.667
They've been in my family
for generations!

04:04.747 --> 04:06.207
Oh, really?

04:06.297 --> 04:08.797
[KAHN] The great Dainsleif
and Valhalla,

04:08.877 --> 04:11.717
both of which were made
by my ancestor.

04:11.797 --> 04:12.967
Over the centuries,

04:13.047 --> 04:15.177
countless warriors
have tried and failed

04:15.257 --> 04:16.467
to harness their might.

04:17.057 --> 04:19.057
But 130 years ago,

04:19.137 --> 04:22.517
a man named Pagma was able
to realize their potential.

04:23.357 --> 04:24.937
As the legend goes,

04:25.017 --> 04:26.897
he became one
with the armaments,

04:26.987 --> 04:28.647
understood their abilities,

04:28.737 --> 04:31.107
and performed
a beautiful sword dance.

04:31.487 --> 04:33.657
Yet, he left 'em behind.

04:34.327 --> 04:36.117
He said their chosen owner

04:36.197 --> 04:38.617
would one day walk
through these doors.

04:40.957 --> 04:43.247
Yeah, duh,
and I am that chosen one.

04:43.327 --> 04:45.377
Pagma's Successor
in the house, bitches!

04:45.457 --> 04:46.337
[gasps]

04:47.207 --> 04:49.417
Yes, indeed. Huh.

04:49.507 --> 04:51.797
You were able
to use those armaments

04:51.887 --> 04:52.967
against the Mero Company.

04:54.177 --> 04:55.597
Let's just say,

04:55.677 --> 04:57.967
-if you are Pagma's Successor...
-Hmm.

04:58.057 --> 05:00.977
...it falls to you
to prove the legend true.

05:01.057 --> 05:02.347
Huh?

05:02.437 --> 05:03.897
[GAME VOICE] System guidance.

05:03.977 --> 05:06.357
A legendary job quest
has been generated.

05:06.897 --> 05:08.237
"Prove the Legend."

05:08.897 --> 05:10.777
This is a multi-part quest

05:10.857 --> 05:12.857
involving
the legendary blacksmith, Pagma.

05:12.947 --> 05:15.617
Successfully completing
all parts of the quest

05:15.697 --> 05:17.787
will give you the power
to change the world.

05:17.867 --> 05:21.207
[TAKUMI] Oh, man,
"Reward: Unknown" is diabolical!

05:21.287 --> 05:22.367
You're telling me one day,

05:22.667 --> 05:24.827
this legendary set
is destined to be mine?

05:24.917 --> 05:25.787
In that case...

05:26.337 --> 05:28.167
Gimme them shits right now!

05:28.257 --> 05:30.457
[KAHN] A face
only a blind mother could love.

05:30.547 --> 05:33.837
You know, you really
don't act like the successor.

05:33.927 --> 05:35.047
Hey!

05:35.427 --> 05:37.597
Shut up, man, I'mma prove
the dick off that legend!

05:37.677 --> 05:39.637
Now teach me
how to be a blacksmith!

05:39.717 --> 05:42.807
[chuckles] My word,
you're in quite the hurry.

05:43.347 --> 05:46.397
First thing we need to do
is rebuild the forge.

05:46.477 --> 05:49.727
Just be warned,
the Mero Company may return.

05:50.397 --> 05:51.527
[sips]

05:53.567 --> 05:54.607
Rabbit.

05:55.197 --> 05:58.987
I assume things are proceeding
accordingly with the forge?

05:59.077 --> 06:02.117
Indeed. All the pieces
are falling into place.

06:02.197 --> 06:04.417
What is taking so damned long?!

06:04.497 --> 06:07.077
Tear that hovel apart
if you must, just get it done!

06:07.167 --> 06:08.917
The local lord, Earl Steim,

06:08.997 --> 06:10.837
would likely
not appreciate that.

06:10.917 --> 06:12.207
We must do our utmost

06:12.297 --> 06:14.837
to avoid damaging
the Mero Company's reputation.

06:15.427 --> 06:17.337
Ah. That, we must.

06:17.427 --> 06:20.177
Now then, tell me
about your new plan.

06:21.677 --> 06:23.847
Let's just say
that I've hired the right man.

06:24.477 --> 06:27.187
A man who's blessed
with what one might call...

06:27.267 --> 06:28.937
a golden tongue.

06:33.397 --> 06:35.987
[VILLAGER] So he's the one
who killed Veil's men?

06:36.737 --> 06:38.987
Boy's barely old enough
to hold a hammer.

06:39.617 --> 06:41.407
He's brilliant, I assure you.

06:41.487 --> 06:43.537
Though, I'll admit,
he does look a bit slow.

06:43.617 --> 06:44.827
[TAKUMI] Okay,
you know what, man?

06:44.907 --> 06:46.667
I'm like, right here.

06:46.747 --> 06:48.917
Oi, Kahn! Did you see this?

06:50.247 --> 06:52.757
Mero Company recruitment poster?

06:52.837 --> 06:55.047
Yeah, apparently
they're lookin' for workers

06:55.127 --> 06:56.887
at the new shop
they just opened up.

06:56.967 --> 06:59.597
You know, I have to say,
the pay is decent.

06:59.677 --> 07:00.717
[scoffs]

07:00.807 --> 07:03.927
[all protesting]

07:04.847 --> 07:06.437
-[MAN] Excuse me.
-[ALL] Huh?

07:06.517 --> 07:07.977
I'm guessing
you must be the gentlemen

07:08.057 --> 07:09.807
whose businesses
the Mero Company bought

07:09.897 --> 07:10.857
for next to nothing.

07:11.317 --> 07:13.397
Did they make you
an offer you couldn't refuse?

07:14.147 --> 07:16.857
[TAKUMI] This guy.
He's a player, like me.

07:16.947 --> 07:18.737
Get out of here, you outsider!

07:18.817 --> 07:20.737
I bet you're a spy for Mero!

07:20.817 --> 07:23.907
Me? Oh, no. I'm here
with some friendly advice.

07:23.997 --> 07:25.617
Right now,
all the local businesses

07:25.697 --> 07:26.707
are hurting for workers.

07:27.157 --> 07:29.377
Mero's no exception,
and they're not going anywhere,

07:29.457 --> 07:30.877
which means stable income.

07:30.957 --> 07:32.547
If you can't beat them,
I'd say join them.

07:33.167 --> 07:34.337
That's a good point.

07:34.417 --> 07:36.047
Hmm. The lad's right.

07:36.717 --> 07:38.337
It's the same idea
with this forge.

07:38.427 --> 07:39.967
You could keep your name
on the deed

07:40.047 --> 07:41.387
and let your business fail,

07:41.467 --> 07:43.387
or you could sign it
over to Mero.

07:43.467 --> 07:44.677
[TAKUMI] What is this?

07:45.307 --> 07:48.137
-His vibes are so off.
-It's a win-win for everybody.

07:48.227 --> 07:49.687
[all gasp]

07:49.767 --> 07:52.607
For an outsider, you've taken
quite an interest in us.

07:52.687 --> 07:53.607
What's your name, lad?

07:54.777 --> 07:57.357
Well, you can
just call me Huroi.

07:57.447 --> 07:58.447
Huroi.

07:58.527 --> 07:59.697
Maybe you're right,

07:59.777 --> 08:01.617
working
with a larger organization

08:01.697 --> 08:03.157
could be beneficial.

08:03.237 --> 08:04.367
But in this village,

08:04.447 --> 08:06.287
there's such a thing
as peasants' rights.

08:06.367 --> 08:07.827
And what might those be?

08:07.907 --> 08:09.667
A law enacted for the people

08:09.747 --> 08:12.577
by Earl Steim,
our benevolent lord.

08:12.667 --> 08:15.337
Locals have the right
to access information

08:15.417 --> 08:17.587
about the region
before anyone else.

08:17.667 --> 08:20.467
Any information
that could benefit our lives,

08:20.547 --> 08:22.677
we're guaranteed to see first.

08:23.217 --> 08:26.637
The earl puts our livelihoods
before that of any outsider.

08:26.717 --> 08:28.687
Then came the Mero Company.

08:28.767 --> 08:30.437
They colluded
with the local lords

08:30.517 --> 08:33.307
to unlawfully keep
the information for themselves.

08:33.397 --> 08:36.397
That goes directly
against the will of the earl.

08:37.187 --> 08:39.147
Which is why
it cannot be allowed.

08:39.237 --> 08:40.317
Hmm.

08:40.397 --> 08:41.867
Yes, I see your point.

08:42.617 --> 08:43.577
Well, then.

08:43.907 --> 08:45.527
I'll take it upon myself
to go tell the earl

08:45.617 --> 08:47.247
of the Mero Company's misdeeds.

08:47.787 --> 08:49.287
If what you're saying is true,

08:49.367 --> 08:51.327
then I think it's time
you all got some justice.

08:52.077 --> 08:53.587
That's what I like to hear!

08:53.667 --> 08:55.417
Thank you
for helping with our cause!

08:55.957 --> 08:59.877
Well, perhaps you're kinder
than I gave you credit for.

09:00.547 --> 09:02.427
[TAKUMI] Oh, what the hell?

09:02.507 --> 09:05.887
He's a player, but somehow
he's controlling the NPCs!

09:05.967 --> 09:08.267
He just changed the flow
of the conversation

09:08.347 --> 09:10.097
and got them
to give him a new quest!

09:13.187 --> 09:15.057
[Takumi panting] Hey!

09:15.937 --> 09:16.977
Hmm?

09:18.107 --> 09:19.317
What's up, man?

09:19.817 --> 09:20.987
I'm onto you.

09:21.067 --> 09:22.317
You were gonna shill
for the Mero Company

09:22.397 --> 09:23.357
when you showed up.

09:23.907 --> 09:26.407
So how'd you change your quest
to join the other side?

09:26.487 --> 09:28.997
Oh, so you noticed that.

09:29.077 --> 09:31.247
Answer the question, dickbag!

09:31.327 --> 09:33.497
All right, you got me.

09:33.577 --> 09:35.207
I realized
there was more in it for me

09:35.287 --> 09:36.627
if I helped the villagers.

09:36.707 --> 09:39.087
This game's
the ultimate sandbox, after all.

09:39.167 --> 09:41.507
If you get wrapped up
in the NPC's lives,

09:41.587 --> 09:42.837
sometimes you'll get lucky,

09:42.927 --> 09:44.587
and it'll trigger
a hidden quest.

09:44.677 --> 09:46.297
Sorta like this one.

09:46.387 --> 09:48.097
Share my quest info, please.

09:48.967 --> 09:50.137
Hmm?

09:50.727 --> 09:52.557
Dude! That reward is insane!

09:52.637 --> 09:54.897
I didn't know you could
change mid-stream like that!

09:54.977 --> 09:55.977
[laughs]

09:56.057 --> 09:57.857
I'm not surprised
you're surprised!

09:57.937 --> 10:00.027
Only the hardcore vets
who've played since the launch

10:00.107 --> 10:01.107
would know this stuff.

10:01.647 --> 10:04.607
Bro! I happen to be one of
those hardcore vets, okay?!

10:04.697 --> 10:06.697
I've been playing
this shit since vanilla!

10:06.777 --> 10:08.527
[laughs]

10:08.617 --> 10:10.577
-You're hilarious! [chuckles]
-Shut up!

10:10.657 --> 10:11.907
You want some of this?!

10:11.997 --> 10:14.077
I've really enjoyed
this little chat,

10:14.157 --> 10:16.207
but I have somewhere
I need to be.

10:16.287 --> 10:17.537
See ya around!

10:17.627 --> 10:20.417
I sure hope not!
Bye forever, you bitch!

10:26.257 --> 10:27.387
I can do this.

10:27.467 --> 10:29.427
I'll clear this quest
no matter what.

10:35.597 --> 10:36.897
[gasps]

10:40.437 --> 10:41.437
[sighs]

10:42.147 --> 10:45.107
You'll gain nothing by wasting
your time on the earl, you know.

10:47.197 --> 10:49.277
Perhaps you misheard my request.

10:49.367 --> 10:51.537
I asked you to persuade
Kahn and the villagers

10:51.617 --> 10:53.577
to hand over that forge.

10:56.367 --> 10:58.167
Relax.
I wasn't going to follow through

10:58.247 --> 10:59.747
on what I'd promised them.

10:59.837 --> 11:00.917
The art of persuasion

11:00.997 --> 11:02.837
is about making people
feel at ease.

11:02.917 --> 11:06.887
[chuckles] I expected you
to be a better liar.

11:06.967 --> 11:07.927
[grunts]

11:09.047 --> 11:11.927
You renounced your freedom
the moment you betrayed us.

11:12.557 --> 11:14.177
Take him to the dungeon.

11:20.517 --> 11:22.727
How did he find out?

11:23.477 --> 11:25.237
I finally get the secret quest,

11:25.317 --> 11:28.067
and then, of course,
this is how it plays out for me.

11:28.157 --> 11:29.237
[GAME VOICE] System guidance.

11:29.317 --> 11:32.157
-Your current quest has changed.
-What?

11:32.237 --> 11:34.117
[GAME VOICE] Your new quest
is, "Waiting"...

11:34.197 --> 11:35.747
[HUROI] The quest changed again?

11:35.827 --> 11:37.037
No way.

11:37.117 --> 11:38.957
Is this the real hidden quest?

11:39.827 --> 11:41.287
Eight game days?!

11:41.377 --> 11:43.457
That's 50 hours real time!

11:44.417 --> 11:45.507
What the hell?

11:45.587 --> 11:47.757
The most I've ever
been able to do is 20!

11:48.797 --> 11:50.177
50 hours.

11:50.507 --> 11:53.137
If anything abnormal happens
to my brainwaves,

11:53.217 --> 11:54.967
the game
will automatically log me out

11:55.057 --> 11:56.387
whether I like it or not!

11:57.177 --> 11:59.267
And then I'll have nothing left!

12:18.577 --> 12:20.747
I'll clear this quest
no matter what.

12:22.247 --> 12:23.997
Apostle of Justice.

12:24.087 --> 12:25.547
I'll be right here!

12:30.297 --> 12:32.347
[HINAKO] Quest B-408 has begun.

12:32.427 --> 12:34.927
We need to call
an emergency board meeting.

12:37.597 --> 12:39.387
So, what is B-408?

12:39.477 --> 12:42.307
Well, apparently
it's a hidden S-rank quest.

12:42.397 --> 12:44.147
Must take something special
to pop.

12:44.227 --> 12:47.937
Yes, and if it's completed,
the results are special as well.

12:48.027 --> 12:51.237
It will give us the first
Satisfy user with two jobs.

12:51.857 --> 12:53.617
Until now,
people have only been focused

12:53.697 --> 12:55.827
on hunting down the rarest jobs,

12:55.907 --> 12:58.447
but once they figure out
that second jobs exist,

12:58.537 --> 13:00.497
that focus
will change dramatically.

13:01.037 --> 13:03.747
This goes beyond the bounds
of a special quest.

13:03.837 --> 13:06.167
It could reshape
the future of Satisfy.

13:10.127 --> 13:12.927
[HINAKO] The ID of the player
attempting Quest B-408

13:13.007 --> 13:14.847
appears to be "Huroi."

13:14.927 --> 13:17.427
He's a 24-year-old man
from Mongolia,

13:17.507 --> 13:19.887
real name Damb Allunbatar.

13:19.977 --> 13:22.727
He is currently
a level-126 orator.

13:23.477 --> 13:26.647
To date, his longest
continuous login was 20 hours.

13:27.647 --> 13:30.147
During that session,
his vitals stayed within range,

13:30.237 --> 13:33.067
but the psychological stress
appeared to take a toll.

13:33.157 --> 13:34.867
It was severe enough
to nearly trigger

13:34.947 --> 13:36.657
the capsule's forced log-out.

13:37.697 --> 13:38.827
Given this data,

13:39.197 --> 13:41.077
we estimate that his chance
of completing the quest

13:41.157 --> 13:43.367
would be roughly 9%.

13:43.957 --> 13:45.167
So much for that.

13:45.247 --> 13:47.377
That's way too dangerous
to even attempt.

13:47.457 --> 13:49.797
[HINAKO] In addition,
the Apostle of Justice

13:49.877 --> 13:53.757
whose job it is to save Huroi,
is supposed to be an NPC, but...

13:54.137 --> 13:55.717
A new variable appeared.

13:55.797 --> 13:57.927
Caught us
completely by surprise.

13:58.557 --> 14:01.097
[SAKAEDA] Huroi shared
the quest with another player,

14:01.177 --> 14:02.927
and now the game
is treating that player

14:03.017 --> 14:04.477
as the Apostle of Justice.

14:05.097 --> 14:08.397
Problem is, our new Apostle
doesn't know about his new role.

14:08.477 --> 14:09.477
[YAZAKI] So, what?

14:09.567 --> 14:11.187
Is having
another player save him

14:11.277 --> 14:13.447
instead of an NPC
really an issue?

14:14.067 --> 14:15.317
Take a look at this.

14:15.407 --> 14:18.327
If we track the direction
this NPC is headed,

14:18.407 --> 14:19.827
we can develop a theory.

14:21.117 --> 14:23.867
A theory that revolves
around another player,

14:23.957 --> 14:26.417
the person who unlocked
the third epic class.

14:29.457 --> 14:30.707
[RABBIT] Personally,

14:31.087 --> 14:33.917
I've never been the sort who
puts much faith in coincidence.

14:34.417 --> 14:36.717
But if this works,
I won't shy away.

14:42.387 --> 14:43.677
[bird cries]

14:46.807 --> 14:49.147
[PLAYER 1] Come on!
Join our party, please!

14:49.227 --> 14:51.817
[PLAYER 2] No, screw those guys!
You should join us.

14:51.897 --> 14:53.357
We're begging you!

14:53.437 --> 14:54.737
[ALL PLAYERS] Euphemina!

14:54.817 --> 14:56.777
Aww, you're all too sweet!

14:56.857 --> 14:58.407
But there's so many of you.

14:58.487 --> 15:00.487
How will I ever choose?

15:00.577 --> 15:04.617
I guess I could join
whoever kills the most mobs.

15:04.707 --> 15:06.157
[all exclaim]

15:06.247 --> 15:08.377
[PLAYER 3] Out of our way!
Euphemina's coming with us!

15:08.457 --> 15:10.627
[PLAYER 4]
No, she's coming with us!

15:10.707 --> 15:13.257
Suck on my Explosive Veil!

15:13.707 --> 15:15.217
Lightning Slice!

15:16.297 --> 15:17.717
[sighs]

15:17.797 --> 15:20.677
Mid, mid, and more mid.
That’s just great.

15:20.757 --> 15:22.927
[player 5 yells]

15:23.387 --> 15:25.887
Frenzied Spiral!

15:27.267 --> 15:29.727
Okay. Now that I can work with!

15:29.807 --> 15:31.687
[yells]

15:32.817 --> 15:34.857
[EUPHEMINA] Skill Copy.

15:44.577 --> 15:47.117
[GAME VOICE]
Your Skill Copy was successful.

15:47.207 --> 15:49.787
Skill will be stored
until you use it once.

15:50.327 --> 15:51.537
[Euphemina chuckles]

15:51.627 --> 15:54.707
Another lovely day
to be an epic class.

15:54.797 --> 15:56.377
[player 6 sighs]

15:57.167 --> 15:59.467
So what do you say,
do you wanna join our party--

16:00.507 --> 16:02.467
What the hell? Euphemina?

16:04.007 --> 16:05.517
[EUPHEMINA] Condemn
the Red Knight Traitor,

16:05.597 --> 16:06.847
S-rank quest.

16:07.387 --> 16:10.727
Find and condemn the former
knight commander, Piaro.

16:11.727 --> 16:13.267
I think I may
finally have what I need

16:13.357 --> 16:14.727
to beat this stupid quest.

16:15.527 --> 16:16.937
[footsteps approaching]

16:17.027 --> 16:18.567
Can I help you?

16:18.647 --> 16:21.237
You know it's rude
to stare at strangers, right?

16:21.317 --> 16:22.697
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

16:22.777 --> 16:25.287
You mean to tell me
that you've forgotten who I am?

16:25.367 --> 16:26.947
Wow, that one's in the running

16:27.037 --> 16:28.327
for the worst pickup line
of all time.

16:28.407 --> 16:30.957
Tell me, does the name
Erina sound familiar?

16:32.037 --> 16:33.537
After witnessing her talents,

16:33.627 --> 16:36.757
the Mero Company hired her
as their new blacksmith,

16:36.837 --> 16:39.467
but she vanished
after taking their advance.

16:39.547 --> 16:41.587
She had lied to them
about everything,

16:41.677 --> 16:43.257
even her true identity.

16:44.007 --> 16:46.427
Euphemina the Duplicator.

16:49.057 --> 16:50.227
[sighs]

16:50.307 --> 16:52.147
I haven't told
any of the other players

16:52.227 --> 16:53.437
about that, you know.

16:53.517 --> 16:55.727
Can you NPCs hack
into our data now?

16:56.267 --> 16:58.687
Afraid I can
neither confirm nor deny,

16:59.187 --> 17:02.157
but I do wonder why you're
in such a hurry to escape.

17:03.407 --> 17:04.527
Look, dude.

17:04.947 --> 17:07.287
I'm kind of in the middle
of a major quest right now.

17:07.907 --> 17:09.537
Someone's gotta take down Piaro,

17:09.617 --> 17:11.867
the top knight
of the Saharan Empire,

17:11.957 --> 17:14.997
and naturally, I happen
to be the one for the job.

17:15.627 --> 17:16.917
[RABBIT] You were the one,

17:16.997 --> 17:19.207
but you're going to
have to abandon that quest.

17:19.297 --> 17:20.257
Excuse me?

17:20.337 --> 17:21.757
Because currently,

17:21.837 --> 17:24.047
I'd like your help
with another quest.

17:24.137 --> 17:26.347
[Euphemina scoffs]
"Difficulty unknown"?

17:26.427 --> 17:27.467
Correct.

17:27.557 --> 17:29.977
You are an NPC.
You can't threaten me!

17:30.057 --> 17:32.057
One could perceive it
as a threat,

17:32.137 --> 17:34.517
but these conditions
are good for you, no?

17:39.527 --> 17:40.937
Huroi was arrested?

17:41.027 --> 17:42.237
He was.

17:42.317 --> 17:44.907
Under suspicion
of treason against the Earl.

17:44.987 --> 17:48.537
He's being kept in the castle's
underground dungeon right now.

17:49.447 --> 17:51.037
You think it's
because of those assholes?

17:51.117 --> 17:53.207
Yeah. Damn Mero Company

17:53.287 --> 17:55.327
has some crafty ones
workin' for 'em.

17:55.417 --> 17:56.787
-[knock on door]
-Hmm?

18:00.667 --> 18:02.047
Pardon me.

18:02.127 --> 18:05.137
My name is Rabbit,
and I'm with the Mero Company.

18:05.757 --> 18:09.137
I've come here to speak with you
on behalf of my master, Valmont.

18:11.597 --> 18:12.847
[Kahn sighs]

18:12.927 --> 18:15.857
So then,
if we want Huroi to be freed,

18:15.937 --> 18:18.067
we must accept your terms?

18:18.147 --> 18:19.607
[RABBIT] That is correct, yes.

18:19.687 --> 18:21.607
Hah! That dumb idiot can rot

18:21.687 --> 18:23.697
in that stink-hole
for all I care!

18:23.777 --> 18:25.697
A touching display of kindness.

18:25.777 --> 18:27.197
All motives aside,

18:27.277 --> 18:29.907
the fact is, Huroi did try
to protect the villagers.

18:30.737 --> 18:33.827
He went to speak to the Earl,
regardless of the danger,

18:33.907 --> 18:36.457
and you're just
going to abandon him?

18:36.537 --> 18:37.837
[KAHN] Hmm.

18:37.917 --> 18:39.207
Now, of course,

18:39.297 --> 18:41.497
I wouldn't ask you
to simply hand over the forge

18:41.587 --> 18:42.957
in exchange for his freedom.

18:44.877 --> 18:45.887
I'd like to challenge you

18:46.257 --> 18:48.717
to an item-crafting match
with the Mero Company.

18:48.797 --> 18:49.847
-The hell?
-You what?

18:49.927 --> 18:51.887
If you win,
we will cease all attempts

18:51.967 --> 18:53.677
at acquiring your forge.

18:53.767 --> 18:55.267
And, of course,

18:55.347 --> 18:56.807
we'll release Huroi.

18:56.897 --> 18:59.147
Hmm. Very well then.

18:59.227 --> 19:02.477
Just know,
I will not be participating.

19:02.567 --> 19:05.487
Instead,
I nominate Pagma's Successor.

19:05.567 --> 19:07.697
-[gasps]
-Pagma's Successor?

19:07.777 --> 19:09.237
My apprentice, Grid.

19:09.327 --> 19:11.037
Hey! Who said
you could volunteer me?!

19:11.117 --> 19:12.327
[GAME VOICE] System guidance.

19:12.617 --> 19:15.747
Quest, "Item Creation Match
with the Mero Company"

19:15.827 --> 19:16.997
has been generated.

19:17.377 --> 19:21.417
-[TAKUMI] 600 gold?!
- Will you accept this quest?

19:22.497 --> 19:23.587
Quest accepted.

19:24.207 --> 19:26.837
You just yee'd your last haw,
you creepy-ass, four-eyed dick!

19:26.927 --> 19:28.427
Perhaps I have.

19:28.507 --> 19:29.547
But I know for a fact

19:29.637 --> 19:31.427
that you are not
Pagma's Successor,

19:31.507 --> 19:34.137
and I intend to secure
the proof of that.

19:34.217 --> 19:36.557
The match will be in three days.
Is that acceptable?

19:36.637 --> 19:38.647
[TAKUMI] Hell yeah,
your shit's about to get rocked!

19:38.727 --> 19:41.107
That 72,000 yen is mine, boi!

19:46.487 --> 19:48.907
[Huroi groaning softly]

19:48.987 --> 19:51.947
Finally, halfway there.

19:55.157 --> 19:56.907
I'm gonna do this.

19:56.997 --> 20:00.127
I refuse to give in now.

20:02.877 --> 20:05.047
[TAKUMI] You clowns bet
on the wrong pony!

20:05.127 --> 20:07.587
I'm the legendary blacksmith!

20:07.667 --> 20:09.677
They can kiss
my legendary class.

20:09.757 --> 20:11.217
Time to hammer down!

20:15.307 --> 20:17.517
Greetings, one and all!

20:17.597 --> 20:19.807
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for joining us,

20:19.887 --> 20:24.777
and welcome to the Mero Company
spectacular Item-Creation Match!

20:24.857 --> 20:26.727
[crowd cheering]

20:26.817 --> 20:28.067
And now, friends,

20:28.147 --> 20:30.817
allow me to introduce
our challengers!

20:31.447 --> 20:33.277
You're confident
we can win this, right?

20:33.367 --> 20:34.407
Of course, sir.

20:34.487 --> 20:36.947
[JUDGE]
Representing Kahn's Forge,

20:37.037 --> 20:38.117
Grid!

20:38.197 --> 20:39.537
Grid, you can do it!

20:39.617 --> 20:41.167
[VILLAGER] We believe in you!

20:41.247 --> 20:43.707
[JUDGE] And representing
the Mero Company,

20:43.787 --> 20:45.337
Erina!

20:45.417 --> 20:48.047
[crowd cheering]

20:48.127 --> 20:50.047
Thanks for the support,
everyone!

20:55.347 --> 20:58.927
[fans chanting]
Erina! Erina! Erina!

20:59.017 --> 21:00.387
-Erina!
-And Grid!

21:01.477 --> 21:03.267
[SAKAEDA]
And they're off and running.

21:03.357 --> 21:05.767
This tournament
will determine Huroi's fate.

21:06.727 --> 21:10.107
Hinako, are we in touch
with Satisfy's Mongolian branch?

21:10.197 --> 21:11.357
Yes, sir.

21:11.447 --> 21:13.317
The local personnel
is ready to intervene

21:13.407 --> 21:15.867
if the worst-case scenario
happens.

21:16.327 --> 21:18.237
Hmm. Now, then.

21:19.367 --> 21:21.497
The success of Quest B-408,

21:21.577 --> 21:23.877
and Satisfy's
first-ever second job

21:24.837 --> 21:27.127
rests entirely
on Grid's shoulders.

21:28.167 --> 21:30.047
-[EUPHEMINA] Hello there, Grid!
-Hmm?

21:30.127 --> 21:32.377
It's such a pleasure
to meet you.

21:32.467 --> 21:35.547
Ugh, gross.
What are you, kid, like 12?

21:35.637 --> 21:36.887
[gasps]

21:36.967 --> 21:39.267
What are you talking about?
I'm 19 years old!

21:39.347 --> 21:40.847
What gives you
the right to be so rude?!

21:40.927 --> 21:43.347
Well, I passed sixth grade,
for starters.

21:43.437 --> 21:46.357
-[scoffs] That's a surprise.
-"Goo-goo-ga-ga" to you too.

21:46.437 --> 21:47.437
[hisses]

21:47.527 --> 21:48.607
[hisses]

21:48.687 --> 21:51.187
[both growling]

21:51.277 --> 21:53.697
Uh, let's try
to keep things civil, now!

21:55.067 --> 21:56.197
Uh, right then!

21:56.277 --> 21:59.037
Let the match begin!

21:59.117 --> 22:03.207
[♪ tense music playing]

22:09.997 --> 22:12.337
[♪ closing theme song playing]
